Subject: Make virtual joysticks the layer's own on every platform
Upstream-base: fbe120f5020f8bdcb9cbf5ae28d9859b29781119

The host makes every player a virtual Wii Remote: desktop_wpad.cpp attaches a
virtual gamepad with an accelerometer and wpad_sdl.cpp turns its sensor events
into WPAD reports. SDL2's virtual joysticks have no sensors, and on Switch there
were none, so the game had no input there. The layer now keeps its own virtual
devices, as SDL3's software driver does, in one implementation for every
platform; the joystick and gamepad calls choose between them and the platform's
devices. Their events pass the app's filter and watches as SDL3's do, gamepad
event first, but not SDL2's own watches. The libnx pads queue theirs that way
too.

