-- Virtual joysticks have no sensors, so `SDL_SendJoystickVirtualSensorData` fails.
+- Virtual joysticks are the layer's own on every platform and behave as SDL3's software driver
+  makes them, with their gamepad view, rumble, LEDs, effects, sensors and player numbers. Balls and
+  touchpads have no calls to reach them. A virtual gamepad's type is known only for Nintendo's
+  Switch and GameCube controller ids, and a player number a real controller has stays with it.
+  Each virtual gamepad is mapped from its own descriptor, where SDL3 reuses the mapping it made for
+  the first one with the same name and ids.
